# Development defaults for `next dev`. No secrets: everything here is public by
# construction (NEXT_PUBLIC_*) and matches what Compose already injects.
#
# Without this, lib/ws.ts falls back to window.location.origin and the browser
# opens ws://localhost:4242/ws — a path Next does not serve and cannot proxy,
# because rewrites do not carry WebSocket upgrades. The socket 404s, the store
# retries, and the incident room silently loses every live event while the
# reconnect loop runs. Compose never hit it because it sets the variable.
# `next dev` cannot proxy WebSocket upgrades through a rewrite. Point the
# browser directly at the local API so incident timelines receive live events.
NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL=ws://localhost:8080/ws
